# What the build context may contain. Passed explicitly:
#
#   docker build --file infra/container/Dockerfile --ignorefile infra/container/Dockerfile.dockerignore .
#
# It lives under `infra/container/` rather than at the repository root because the root is the
# coordination checkout, which this card does not write; an ignore file placed there would be a
# change to a shared file. Naming it explicitly also makes the exclusion visible in the build
# command rather than depending on a file an operator might not notice.

# Everything, then the few things the build actually needs. A default-allow list would have to
# anticipate every file the checkout may grow, and one missed entry would ship it into an image.
**

# The two inputs of the locked resolution, plus the source that gets installed.
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!src/**

# The source is narrowed too: only modules are installed, so a stray scratch file under `src/` is
# not carried in. Nothing outside `src/tianshu_memory/` is needed.
src/**
!src/tianshu_memory/**
src/tianshu_memory/**
!src/tianshu_memory/*.py
!src/tianshu_memory/**/*.py

# The probe script is copied in its own layer, so it is the third and last thing kept.
!scripts/container_healthcheck.py

# Named for what they are, so a reader can see each exclusion was deliberate rather than an
# oversight of a wildcard. The first group is already covered by `**` and stays because the reason
# matters: this image must never contain a checkout, a runtime directory, a credential or a
# database, and a build context that could carry one is one mistake away from doing so.
.git/**
.gitignore
.github/**
.runtime/**
.venv/**
venv/**
tests/**
docs/**
infra/**
projects/**
node_modules/**
__pycache__/**
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/**
.ruff_cache/**

# Local state and credentials, by extension and by name rather than by directory, because a private
# configuration can sit anywhere an operator put it. `*.json` is deliberately not excluded: the
# build inputs are a `.toml` and a `.lock`, and excluding every JSON file would silently drop any
# packaged data file a future module needs. These patterns name the artifacts that hold secrets or
# real content instead.
*.jsonl
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
.env
.env.*
credentials*
*credential*
*secret*
*password*
*token*
source-guard.json

# Container files themselves: the build does not need its own recipe or the build script it runs.
Dockerfile*
*.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
